Note: catching problems instead of stopping the program.

to find the checked age of a number
  if the number is less than 0, fail with "An age can't be negative, but I got" and then the number and then ".".
  give back the number.
that's all.

for every age in (34, -3 and 7)
  try the following.
    say "Age:" and then the checked age of age.
  if something goes wrong
    say "Skipped." and then the error.
  that's all.
that's all.

try to read the file "settings.txt" into settings, and if that fails, set settings to "nothing saved yet".
say "Settings:" and then settings.

set numbers to 10, 0 and 5.
for every n in numbers
  try the following.
    say "100 divided by" and then n and then "is" and then 100 / n.
  if something goes wrong
    say "100 divided by" and then n and then "does not work:" and then the error.
  that's all.
that's all.
